# runs/ is gitignored EXCEPT the committed results: the summary CSVs, the
# figures the README embeds (a gitignored figure is a broken image on GitHub),
# and the diagnostic and distribution JSONs that the headline claims in
# README §5.4 and §5.7 rest on. They are small (~360 KB per set) and none is
# regenerable without the checkpoints and an hour of GPU time.
#
# The diag/dist patterns are GLOBBED (`runs/diag*`) so that a per-corpus
# variant — runs/diag_code/, runs/dist_code/ — is committed automatically. It
# was not, when the second corpus was added, and the JSONs behind §5.7 would
# have been silently dropped from the commit that cited them.
#
# The grids themselves stay ignored at any corpus: runs/quant/ is 300 files and
# runs/quant_code/ another 20, and they are reproducible from the committed
# corpora given the checkpoints.
runs/*
!runs/results/
runs/results/*
!runs/results/*.csv
!runs/results/*.png
!runs/diag*/
runs/diag*/*
!runs/diag*/*.json
!runs/dist*/
runs/dist*/*
!runs/dist*/*.json
# LAMBADA (R8, README §5.8). ~1.1 MB, and the per-example 0/1 arrays inside are
# what make every interval in that section recomputable without a GPU.
!runs/lambada*/
runs/lambada*/*
!runs/lambada*/*.json

# data/ IS committed. The corpus swap moved the headline by ~5x, so the exact
# document set is part of the result, not an input that can be regenerated.
# See data/README.md and README.md §6.

.venv/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.memmap

# Working documents: kept local, not published. The README is the deliverable
# and is self-contained; these are the notebook behind it.
/HANDOFF.md
/LIMITATIONS.md
/attention-sinks-quant-plan.md
